// Cyrus designer WEAPON components (2026-10-12, universal-modder finding 5): hitscan, beam and area_blast for the item /
// ability designer. FIXED Java like the rest of the component library (./java.ts), added to a mod ONLY when one of its
// designs uses a weapon action (like ModelStates), so every existing designer mod keeps its byte-identical sources and
// golden hashes. Every Paper API it calls was checked with javap on paper-api 1.21.1 / 1.21.4 / 1.21.8 / 1.21.11 and
// 26.2 (2026-10-12): World.rayTrace(Location, Vector, double, FluidCollisionMode, boolean, double, Predicate<Entity>),
// World.rayTraceBlocks(Location, Vector, double, FluidCollisionMode, boolean), RayTraceResult.getHitEntity /
// getHitPosition, LivingEntity.setNoDamageTicks(int) / getEyeLocation, Damageable.damage(double, Entity) (via Effects),
// World.spawnParticle(Particle, Location, int, double, double, double, double), Vector.getCrossProduct.
//
// Mechanics that bite (field notes, second hand, kept because they are vanilla rules the API cannot hide):
//   - a shotgun's pellets must be SUMMED per target and dealt as one hit, and the target's hurt-invulnerability reset
//     (setNoDamageTicks(0)), or vanilla's 10-tick invulnerability swallows most pellets / the next shots;
//   - a ray stops at the first block (World.rayTrace returns the nearer of the block and the entity hit);
//   - FULL-AUTO is not possible server-side: the client only repeats a held right-click every 4 ticks (5 shots/s) and
//     sends no "button held" state, so the fastest server-side fire rate is that repeat. Real full-auto needs a client
//     mod sending its own fire packets (the client-mod lane). The validator therefore requires cooldownTicks >= 4 for a
//     weapon on a click trigger (spec.ts WEAPON_LIMITS.minClickCooldown).
// Lag-bomb proof: rays and line-of-sight checks spend the activation's ACTION budget (64), particles its particle budget
// (512), hits its ENTITY budget (32); fixed caps below; a beam is a chain of single delayed steps (no timer), one live beam
// per player and at most LIVE_BEAMS plugin-wide. Nothing here changes a block (no explosion is ever created).
import { WEAPON_LIMITS } from "../spec";

