// the mechanism ItemsAdder / Oraxen / Nexo / CraftEngine use; implemented here from the documented vanilla mechanism,
// no third-party code). A mod's custom block is a note_block in a RESERVED state: the resource pack's
// blockstates/note_block.json maps that state to the mod's own cube model; every other state keeps the vanilla model.
//
// Reserved states: the 7 mob-head instruments (zombie, skeleton, creeper, dragon, wither_skeleton, piglin, custom_head)
// x 25 notes x powered = 350 states. Vanilla only reaches them when a mob head sits ON a note block and the block updates;
// with Paper's `block-updates.disable-noteblock-updates: true` (config/paper-global.yml; needs a restart) it never does.
// A mod gets one instrument (its "home", by namespace hash, like glyph blocks) = 50 blocks; collisions with another mod's
// home are reported (two mods = one blockstate file, the conflict engine's single-owner pack file rule).
//
// Pure + client-safe: validation, allocation, pack files (blockstate, block models, 1.21.4+ item definitions) and the Java
// support class (place / break / drops / no tuning / no note sounds / piston + explosion protection) for the plugin.
// Server facts verified on real Paper (scripts/cyrus/golden-noteblock-flight.ts); how it LOOKS needs a real client.
